Contract: `CloneCounts` must accept any map type whose underlying type is `map[string]int` and must return the same concrete map type so callers keep methods on their named map type. The implementation is:

```go
type Counts map[string]int

func (c Counts) Total() int {
    n := 0
    for _, v := range c {
        n += v
    }
    return n
}

func CloneCounts[M ~map[string]int](m M) map[string]int {
    out := make(map[string]int, len(m))
    for k, v := range m {
        out[k] = v
    }
    return out
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
